# Normative Terms for Rules

This rule defines how normative terms are interpreted across all rules under `.cursor/rules/`.

## Scope

- This rule applies to **all rule files** contained in `.cursor/rules/`, including both existing and future rules.
- All such rules are understood as **regulating the behavior of the AI assistant** that operates in this repository.

## Interpretation of normative terms

- Normative terms such as **MUST**, **MUST NOT**, **SHALL**, **SHALL NOT**, **SHOULD**, **SHOULD NOT**, and **MAY** used in any rule file under `.cursor/rules/` **MUST** be interpreted in accordance with the meanings defined in:
  - [RFC 2119](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2119)
  - [RFC 8174](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8174)
- This interpretation **MUST** be applied consistently and without exception when reading or applying any rule in `.cursor/rules/`.
